From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:46:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/deinterlace_v4l2m2m: timestamps in the output time
 base

The output time base is half the input's, a frame per field, but both
frames kept the input's timestamps: the second the input frame's own,
the first the midpoint of the previous and current ones. In the output
time base the second frame sits at twice the input's timestamp and the
first at the sum of the previous and current ones, or one input frame's
duration earlier when there is no previous frame. Duplicate timestamps
reached the muxer, and an output seek dropped every frame.
---
 libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c b/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c
index f47a33b..07a9cb6 100644
--- a/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_deinterlace_v4l2m2m.c
@@ -821,10 +821,14 @@ static int deint_v4l2m2m_dequeue(AVFilterContext *avctx, AVFrame *input_frame)
 
     output_frame_2->flags &= ~AV_FRAME_FLAG_INTERLACED;
 
-    if (ctx->prev_in_frame && ctx->prev_in_frame->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE
-       && input_frame->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE) {
-      first_pts = (ctx->prev_in_frame->pts + input_frame->pts) / 2;
-      av_log(priv, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "calculated first pts %"PRId64"\n", first_pts);
+    /* the output time base is half the input's: a frame per field */
+    if (input_frame->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE) {
+        output_frame_2->pts = input_frame->pts * 2;
+        if (ctx->prev_in_frame && ctx->prev_in_frame->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE)
+            first_pts = ctx->prev_in_frame->pts + input_frame->pts;
+        else
+            first_pts = output_frame_2->pts - FFMAX(input_frame->duration, 1);
+        av_log(priv, AV_LOG_DEBUG, "calculated first pts %"PRId64"\n", first_pts);
     }
 
     output_frame_1->pts = first_pts;
-- 
